1 NOTE {geni:about_me} # _FA1: 1781 2nd Company 3rd Battalion Lancaster Co. Militia 1781
2 CONT
2 CONT # _FA2: 1781 Andreas Ream Captain 8th Class Marcus Montelius Muster roll 2nd Class 1st
2 CONT
2 CONT # _FA3: 1781 Battalion Lancaster Co. Militia
2 CONT
2 CONT # Emigration: Arrived US Port of Philadelphia on the ship Sally
2 CONT
2 CONT # Event: Fact #4 23 AUG 1773 Oath of Allegiance
2 CONT
2 CONT # Burial: Reamstown, Lancaster, Pa
2 CONT
2 CONT # Military Service: Revolutionary War
2 CONT
2 CONT     Frederick Marcus Montelius was born October 25, 1752 in Upper Saxony, Germany. He arrived in Philadelphia on th ship "Sally" from Rotterdam and took his oath of Allegiance August 23, 1773. He was a Lutheran. he married Christi
2 CONC anna Bartholomew in Philadelphia, October 8, 1777. They were married by Reverand Michael Schlatter, Reformed Minister.
2 CONT
2 CONT     The will of Marcus Montelius of Cacallico Township, Lancaster, Pa. Book J page 385 says he was a storekeeper at Reamstown.
2 CONT
