1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In June 1734, leaseholder Petter Wernander wrote to the CA protesting that the farm he leased had been given away to the owner’s relative and his lease had  been terminated. Wernander argued that he should be allow
2 CONC ed to stay at the farm due to the  contract. He ended his petition stating that “[I]f I, against all odds, would be driven from [the farm],  where I have put in so much toil, work and expenses, my welfare will be ruined”. Jezzica 
2 CONC Israelsson:  In consideration of my meagre  circumstances . The language of poverty as a tool for ordinary people in early modern  Sweden  Master thesis, 60 credits, Spring 2016 Departement of History,, Uppsala University
2 CONT
2 CONT Ungefär samtidigt finns en tullnär Wernander i Uppsala domkyrkoförsamling. 
