1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Petter Svensson was a farmer and juryman at Släthult, Misterhult. He married Ingrid Dretzenia on the 21st of October, 1694, in Kristdala parish. She was the daughter of a priest in Vena parish, Nils Dretzenius, and
2 CONC  was born on the 2nd of November, 1672. Petter and Ingrid settled at Släthult, and he was the first known farmer there. He served as a juryman as well. In September of 1706, Petter Svensson sued Brita (surname unknown) of Ströfkli
2 CONC nten because he said she had falsely accused his wife, Ingrid, of having committed adultery with a cavalry captain who had been staying at Petter and Ingrid’s house. Brita claimed that Petter was not the father of his daughter, Ma
2 CONC ria Persdotter. In court, however, Brita apparently admitted that she had lied, and apologized. In October of 1728, Petter was back in court. This time he sued Ingrid Eriksdotter, the wife of a cavalry captain, saying that she had
2 CONC  falsely accused Petter of adultery. The jury decided that the accusation was a conspiracy between Ingrid and Börje Lund, an old enemy of Petter’s (and husband of Petter’s sister, Maria), to try to discredit Petter. The jury found
2 CONC  Petter innocent, and Börje was directed to pay damages to both Petter Svensson and to Ingrid Eriksdotter, who was thought to have been innocently drawn into the case by Börje Lund. In another case, Börje Lund was fined for having
2 CONC  forged Petter’s signature on an inheritance document. Börje was ordered to pay the inheritance money back to Petter with interest. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Petter and Ingrid Dretzenia had ten children. Ingrid Dretzenia died on the 16th of January, 1725, and Petter married for a second time, on the 25th of July, 1725, to the widow Ingrid Jönsdotter, who died on the 2nd of June, 1754, 
2 CONC at Släthult. Two of the ten children of Ingrid and Petter died very young. The unnamed son died the same day he was born, and Kerstin died within a few days of her birth. The tenth child was born when Ingrid was almost 48 years...
2 CONT
