0 @N6000000006127744958@ NOTE Var av norrländsk släkt och en framgångsrik köpman i Örebro samt fogde i Lekebergs härad. I trakten såg han möjligheten att utnyttja skogar och strömmar för anläggande av hamrar och smideshärdar. Kråkfors, Svartå järnbruk, Björkhy
1 CONC tte hytta ochMedskogs masugn anlade han och Bergskollegie privilegier utfärdades 1658. Grubb var en hård man som inte tvekade att vidta handgripliga åtgärder mot konkurrenter och han sades illa hushålla med skogen. Han låg i strid
1 CONC  med brukspatron AndersStensson och Boij på närliggande Ölsboda bruk och Lassåna bruk men var oftast framgångsrik i sina processer. Han dog 81 år gammal och hans sterbhus sålde Svartå bruk till Albin Möller.
0 @N6000000006127057060@ NOTE Adlad 1693 Grubbensköld
0 @N6000000002577050839@ NOTE SOURCE:
1 CONT 1- The records of A R Anderson, Syracuse, Utah, the Ole Anderson
1 CONT Family geneaogist.
1 CONT 2- The records of Owen B Anderson, brother, from whose records this
1 CONT data was extracted.
1 CONT 3- 5 Oct 2000: Ancestral File
1 CONT
1 CONT NOTES:
1 CONT 1- The ordinance data listed for Maria Duraeus was hard to read on the           A.R.Anderson FGR. Data was taken from the Ancestral File report.
1 CONT 2- The place name of Rumskulla and Kristdala are both parishes in Kalmar         county. I will use Rumskulla as it was first on the Ancestral File report.
0 @N6000000002577169887@ NOTE SOURCE:
1 CONT 1- A.R.Anderson had a genealogist do some research in Sweden. Much
1 CONT of the Meurling family lines are from that source. Her name was Ella
1 CONT Heckschert of Upsulla, Sweden.
1 CONT 2- In a letter to dad (Owen), dated 3 Aug 1958, Rebecca Gustaveson
1 CONT Harris cited this source as to where she found the information
1 CONT for the Meurling and Knagg family lines:
1 CONT * Vol 7 pp. 657 "A Swedish Adel (nobility) Kalandar" by K. K.
1 CONT Leyonhufvund, Washington DC.
1 CONT * "Sweden,#24"; p 464 Family History Library; S.C.L., Ut.
1 CONT
1 CONT !NOTES:
1 CONT 1- The ordinance dates were extracted from an FGR that was copied from an        original and in the process the last two digits of the sealing dates were     not copied. The year shown was 194_ , the Ancelstal File supplied the d
1 CONC ate    of 9 JUl 1948.
1 CONT 2- Rebecca has the father's name as Nils Olafson Meurling born 1690
1 CONT in Kristdala, Kalmar, Sweden. "Olofson" is the partranymic
1 CONT surname. "Meurling" is the surname used because of nobility status.
1 CONT 3- From Rebecca Harris;  Place of birth: Kristdala, Kalmar, Sweden.
1 CONT Place of death: Hult Kalmar, Sweden.
1 CONT 4- Rebecca has the father's name as Nils Olafson Meurling born 1690 in           Kristdala, Kalmar, Sweden. "Olofson" is the partranymic surname.              "Meurling" is the surname used because of nobility status.
1 CONT 5- Some notes from Rebecca Harris Gustaveson Records has the
1 CONT birthplace of this person as Dodershult, Krisdala, Kalmar, Sweden.            Dodershult is listed as a village in the Swedish Postal Address Book, and     a parish on my parish/county list. Can Olaf Meurling be born in two       
1 CONC     parishes?? I will not use Dodershult as the birth parish.
1 CONT 6- The name "(Lars)" was listed in some of the Family Group Records as the
1 CONT first given name. I believe that this was just a notation inserted
1 CONT by the compilers to identify the parentage.
1 CONT 7- 1997: An Ancestral File search has this person's name as Lars Olaus           Hakanson Haquine Meurling (ANF:19M5-VRJ) with the same dates and locality
1 CONT that we have.
0 @N6000000002577169451@ NOTE !SOURCES:
1 CONT 1- 17 Jul 1993; This data was picked up from the records of Owen B
1 CONT Anderson.
1 CONT 2- Sweden FH 39 Genealogy Library SLC. Utah
1 CONT
1 CONT !NOTES:
0 @N6000000002577169751@ NOTE SOURCES:
1 CONT 1- 17 Jul 1993; This data was picked up from the records of Owen B
1 CONT Anderson and his brother Arthur R Anderson.
1 CONT 2- Sweden FH 39 Genealogy Library SLC. Utah
1 CONT 3- Swedish Postal Address Book; Microfich in Family History Center.
1 CONT 3- 6 July 2000: Ancestral File print out.
1 CONT
1 CONT NOTES:
1 CONT 1- The ordinance dates were extracted from an FGR that was copied from an        original and in the process the last digit of the sealing dates did not       copy. This relates to the sealing dates for both wives and their       
1 CONC        children. The year shown was 194... so we used 1942 to satisfy our needs.
1 CONT The Ancestral File had the sealing date for Nils and Margaretha as 10 Mar     1944.
1 CONT 2- From Rebecca Harris;  Place of birth: Kristdala, Kalmar, Sweden. The          records we used had Niel's birthplace as Hult, Kalmar, Sweden which cannot    be correct because, according to the Swedish Postal Address Book, there
1 CONC  is    not a village Hult in Kalmar county. There is a village named Hult in a       parish in Jonkoping county. Jonkoping and Kalmar are both in Smaland          province.
1 CONT 3- Rebecca has the father's name as Nils Olafson Meurling born 1690
1 CONT in Kristdala, Kalmar, Sweden. "Olofson" is the partranymic surname.           "Meurling" is the surname used because of nobility status.
1 CONT 4- Sealing to parent year for Nils, 9 JUL .... is difficult to read (A. R.       Anderson records). The Ancestral File has the sealing to parent date as 9     July 1948.
0 @N6000000002577196885@ NOTE !SOURCE:
1 CONT 1- 1992: Records of Owen B Anderson and A.R.Anderson.
1 CONT 2- Ella Heckscher of Upsulla, Sweden. Genealogy researcher.
1 CONT 3- Vol 7; pp. 657; "A Swedish Adel (nobility) Kalandar" by
1 CONT K.K.Leyonhufvund,
1 CONT Washington DC.
1 CONT 4- Family History Library, SLC, Ut; "Sweden, 24"; p 264.
1 CONT 5- Swedish Postal Address book.
1 CONT
1 CONT !NOTES:
1 CONT 1- In a letter to dad (Owen), dated 3 Aug 1958, from Rebecca
1 CONT Gustaveson Harris cited the source on lines 3and 4 as to where she
1 CONT found the information
1 CONT for the Meurling and Knagg family lines.
1 CONT
1 CONT 2- Sealing to parent year (9 JUL ....) is difficult to read, the
1 CONT year 1942 is
1 CONT used is used to override the computer. (A. R. Anderson records)
1 CONT
1 CONT 3- Mangus died in Celyon, India. (A. R. Anderson records).
