0 @N6000000002577169079@ NOTE SOURCE CITATION:
1 CONT 1-  Page: Film #183574; P# 793; IGI Ordinance Index; FamilySearch.
1 CONT 2-  1992: Owen B Anderson family records.
1 CONT 3-  A.R.Anderson had a genealogist do some research in Sweden. Much
1 CONT of the Meurling family lines are from that source. Some of the copies of
1 CONT the records that we had to work from were hard to read.
1 CONT 4-  Swedish Postal Address Book.
1 CONT 5- 5 Oct 2000: Ancestral File report.
1 CONT
1 CONT !NOTES:
1 CONT 1- Some notes from Rebecca Harris Gustaveson Records has the
1 CONT birthplace of this person as Döderhult, Kristdala, Kalmar, Sweden. The        address book does verify this address.
1 CONT 2- The ordinance dates were extracted from an FGR that was copied from an        original and in the process the last two digits of the sealing dates were     not copied. This relates to the sealing dates for both wives and their 
1 CONC        children. The year shown was 194_ so we used 1942 to satisfy our needs.
1 CONT The correct year will be picked up from the IGI.
1 CONT 3- The postal book does not list a "Dodervichshult" or a "Doderkhuler". It
1 CONT does list a Döderhult which is a parish in Kalmar County. This conflicts
1 CONT with the second village name of "Kristdala" which is also a
1 CONT parish in  Kalmar county. Most of the family names list Kristdala as the
1 CONT birthplace.
1 CONT 4- A person can only have one parish as a birth place so inasmuch as Hakan       Larson Meurling's family were residences of Mörlunda, Kalmar, Sweden, I       will use that for his birthplace. That will eliminate two of the three 
1 CONC        parishes that refered to his birthplace.
