0 @N6000000002576996079@ NOTE SOURCE:
1 CONT 1-  1993: Records of Owen B Anderson
1 CONT 2-  Page: Film #183574; P#415; #014676; IGI Ordinance Index.
1 CONT 3-  In a letter to Dad (Owen), dated 3 Aug 1958, Rebecca Gustaveson
1 CONT Harris cited these sources as to where she found the information for the
1 CONT Meurling and Knagg family:  "A Swedish Adel Kalander" (a list of men          having nobility status) Vol 7; p. 657; by K.K.Leyonhufvund, Washington        DC.
1 CONT 4- "Swedish Families"; # 24 p 464; Family History Library, S.C.L.,Ut.
1 CONT
1 CONT NOTES:
1 CONT 1- In the above letter Rebecca states: "We (Rebecca and her brother David)       had Swedish researcher Ella Heskscher, Uppsala, Sweden do some research,      Then we did some reserch in the Los Angeles Genealogy Library. In his  
1 CONC        travels David searched in other libraries and places to find relatives.
1 CONT found our relatives in, during his travels. I spent most of my time in the    Salt Lake Library.
1 CONT 2- Then in 1953-4 I went to the Genealogical Institute and Sven Kindestam,       Sundagen 60 Enskede, Sweden for records on our Ole Anderson lines. All the    names up to 1954 were done under your father's name. Since then I was t
1 CONC he     family representative.
1 CONT 3- Rebecca Gustasveson Harris has the death date as 11 May 1820 and
1 CONT buried 19 May 1820. This would make Barthold 100 yeares old when he died.     Is this correct? The Ancestral File has his death date as 7 May 1788 which    would make him 67 years old.
1 CONT 4- The Ancestral File has Barthold's, and his siblings, birth place as Asby,     Kristdala, Östergotland. The Swedish Postal Book lists the parish of          Kristdala in Kalmar county only. There is an Asby as a parish listed in
1 CONC        Östergotland. I will list only Asby in the birthplace field as all his        siblings have the same birthplace.
