0 @N6000000002577276521@ NOTE SOURCE:
1 CONT 1- Oct 1993: Owen B Anderson records and Arthur R Anderson family records.
1 CONT 2- Research of Ella Hechscher, Swedish Genealogist for Anderson family
1 CONT 3- Ancestral File (TM)
1 CONT
1 CONT !NOTES:
1 CONT 1- Date: Death (17 JAN ) also shown as 7 JAN . (A.R.Anderson records)
1 CONT 2- The birthplace for this person has been changed to agree with all
1 CONT of the  children on this FGR.
1 CONT 3- This FGR has John's deathdate as 2 Jun 1838.
1 CONT 4- I used the term "of Sunds" as the birthplace even though it was
1 CONT not used on this FGR. It was used with the father's birthplace.
1 CONT The children took the surname of Sundius. This seems to be the
1 CONT first time that this family name was used. I am assuming that
1 CONT it is the name of a large estate in Ostergotland, or possibly a location      that the family wanted to be associated with. This often is done in parts     of Sweden. When this is the case, a patronymic surname is not used,       
1 CONC     excepting when a patronymic surname and locality surname are on the
1 CONT original parish document, then the patronymic name is extracted and not       the locality name. In the case of our files, John Vilhelm Michael Sundius     was introduced into our family by marriage and the surname name of Sundius
1 CONC     was used. There was no partonymic names used.
1 CONT
1 CONT 3- A second record was found in Owen B Anderson's collection that
1 CONT has 11 children listed. We only has 2 in our file.
1 CONT 4- A  note at the top of this FGR says that "his family was sealed
1 CONT to her first husband L.P.Holstrom.
1 CONT 5- Magnus George was sealed to his mother Sophia and her second
1 CONT husband, Lars Peter Holstrom.
1 CONT 6- An additiona record from dad's collection has this persons's
1 CONT birthplace as Sandbrukar, Andrarum, Kristianstad, Sw. This is the only FGR    that I have found this birthplace on.
1 CONT 7- December 1999: In doing some further research of this line I find that
1 CONT there is a two generation gap from the father of John Sundius to the next     possible ancestor in the Sundius familues we have in our files. For that      reason I have put all the extra Sundius family records into a seperat file
1 CONC     until we can find a proper connection to this ancestor.
0 @N6000000002577276542@ NOTE !SOURCE:
1 CONT 1- A.R.Anderson family records. Much of the data in our file will come from
1 CONT research directed by him in the USA or Sweden.
1 CONT 2- Oct 1993: These records were found in the Book Of Rememberance of Owen B.
1 CONT Anderson after his death.
1 CONT 3- 1996: Cradled in Sweden; Carl-Eric Johnson, auther; Appendix C, An
1 CONT Alphabetical Index of parishes.
1 CONT 4- Handbook of Genealogy and Templework; Gen. Society of Utah; 1924.
1 CONT !NOTES:
1 CONT 1- I used the term "of Sunds" as the birthplace even though it was not used      on this FGR. It was used with the father's birthplace. The children took      the surname of Sundius. This seems to be the first time that this famil
1 CONC y      name was used. I am assuming that it is the name of a large estate in         Ostergotland, or possibly a location that the family wanted to be             associated with. This often is done in parts of Sweden. When this i
1 CONC s the      case a patronymic surname is not used, excepting when a patronymic surname    and locality surname are on the original parish document, then the            patronymic name is extracted and not the locality name. In the 
1 CONC case of our    files, John Vilhelm Michael Sundius was introduced into our family by         marriage and the surname of Sundius was used. There was no partonymic         names used in this record.
1 CONT Patronymics were used sometimes as we traced this family back through       several generatrions. When I find this I will put the patronymic name in      parenthesis.  (See notes for Petrus Maregi Rivius of Sunds. rin 7194)
1 CONT 2- For this FGR, the patonymic name is Johnson.
1 CONT 3- A second record was found in Owen B Anderson's collection that has 11
1 CONT children listed. We only has 2 in our file.
1 CONT 4- A  note at the top of this FGR says that "his family was sealed to her        first husband L.P.Holstrom.
1 CONT 5- Magnus George was sealed to his mother Sophia and her second husband, Lars
1 CONT Peter Holstrom.
1 CONT 6- 1996: This appendix lists Sund as a parish in Ostergotland county.
1 CONT 7- 1999: The Handbook of Genealogy and Temple Work has a section which           discusses the changes of christian names to latin names. Where as             scandinavia is predominent Lutheran and the clergy was schooled on lati
1 CONC n      it seems logical that some of the christian names would be spelled with       latin references. In the case of this family the surname Sundius could        very well be formed when the family chose to drop the patrynimic su
1 CONC rname      and chose the family name of Sund. Sundi is latin meaning that was            person was the father and Sundius means that they sre the sons of Sundi.
0 @N6000000002577115221@ NOTE SOURCE:
1 CONT 1- Skurup Parish, Malmohus Register.
1 CONT 2- Film #024510; Logab Temple Records; pt 5: p 185
1 CONT 3- Idaho FAlls Temple recoprds (TIB)
1 CONT 4- 1998:  Ancestral File records
1 CONT 5- Swedish Family Histories #39 from the Family History Archives in
1 CONT SAlt Lake City.
1 CONT 6- Ella Heckcher, Uppsala, Sweden, did a lot of research for Arthur
1 CONT R. Anderson which made up a large part of our data base.
1 CONT 7- 29 May 1997: FamilySearch; Ancestral File Report.
1 CONT
1 CONT NOTES:
1 CONT 1-  Birth (Andrarum, Kristianstad) also shown as (Skurup, Malmohus,
1 CONT Sweden.
1 CONT 2-  Ancestral File has the death date as 1785.
1 CONT 3-  October 1993: Reviewed this file with the records of Owen B
1 CONT Anderson. There were two FGR's with Owen B Anderson's records, the
1 CONT first was the same as our file. The other was a record of data
1 CONT recieved from Ella Heckcher to Hannah Anderson Gustaveson's
1 CONT daughter. Ella had Lar's birthplace as Skurup, Malmohus, Sw.
1 CONT Malomohus and Kristianstad county border each other.
1 CONT 4-  Nov 1993: Some corresrondence recieved by Hannah A Gustasevon's
1 CONT heirs from a Svend Kinderstam, a genealogist in Sweden, says
1 CONT that Rev. Holstrom  was born in Skurup, Malmohus, Sweden.
1 CONT 5-  Hannah's heirs had a note saying: "Wife (Sophia Helena)'s temple
1 CONT work was done first in the Logan Temple as "Grandmother Holmstrom"
1 CONT 1894. It was cleared to be done again by (in) her name in 1938.
1 CONT There was no sealing of couples done in the Logan Temple 7 Jul 1885,
1 CONT also from 3 July to 8 July, 1887."
1 CONT 6-  February 1998: I, Robert B. Anderson, have been revewing the Meurling         family records and have noticed that the Rev. Lars Peter Holmstrom died 8     momths before his son Lars Peter Holmstrom, Junior, was born. His wido
1 CONC w       married John Wilhelm Sundius and they had one child who was sealed to         Lars Peter Holmstrom by the Anderson family several years ago.
0 @N6000000002577115308@ NOTE SOURCE:
1 CONT 1- Ancestral File (TM)
1 CONT
1 CONT NOTES:
1 CONT 1- Spelling:  Birth (Kristianstad Lan) also shown as Malmohus Lan.
1 CONT
1 CONT 2- There is no question as to spelling. Both Names are counties
1 CONT (Lans) in Sweden, and Andrarum is a parish in Kristianstad county,
1 CONT not Malmohus county. The Swedish Postal Address Book lists Dalen as
1 CONT a small village or estate in the parish of Andrarum, Kristianstad.
1 CONT Sweden.
1 CONT
1 CONT 3- The temple ordinance dates were from the records of Hannah
1 CONT Gustaveson.
1 CONT
1 CONT 4- A search of the Ancestral File in 1997 lists later ordinance
1 CONT dates than we have and the locality addresses are listed as Dalen,
1 CONT Ahlstad, Malmohous, Sweden. Dalen is listed as a small village (gd)
1 CONT in Andrarum Parish, Kristianstad county, Sweden. The locality for
1 CONT the names on this family group record doesn't seem to researched
1 CONT very accuratly. All themple work was done before 1970.
1 CONT
1 CONT 1- Spelling:  Birth (Kristianstad Lan) also shown as Malmohus Lan.
1 CONT
1 CONT 2- There is no question as to spelling. Both Names are counties (Lans) in Sweden, and Andrarum is a parish in Kristianstad county, not Malmohus county. The Swedish Postal Address Book lists Dalen as a small village or estate in th
1 CONC e parish of Andrarum, Kristianstad. Sweden.
1 CONT
1 CONT 3- The temple ordinance dates were from the records of Hannah Gustaveson.
1 CONT
1 CONT 4- A search of the Ancestral File in 1997 lists later ordinance dates than we have and the locality addresses are listed as Dalen, Ahlstad, Malmohous, Sweden. Dalen is listed as a small village (gd) in Andrarum Parish, Kristiansta
1 CONC d county, Sweden. The locality for the names on this family group record doesn't seem to researched very accuratly. All themple work was done before 1970.
0 @N6000000002577115469@ NOTE SOURCE:
1 CONT 1-  The Ole Anderson Family Genealogy Records
1 CONT 2-  The Book Of Remembrence Of Owen B Anderson
1 CONT 3-  Ancestral File (1998 edition)
1 CONT 4-  Swedish Postal Book
1 CONT
1 CONT NOTES:
1 CONT 1-  Kristianstad and Malmohus are both counties (Lans). Andrarum is a  parish     in Kristianstad.
1 CONT 2-  November 1993: In reveiwing again some record from Owen B  Anderson's         records I found that the FGR compiled by the heirs of Hanna Anderson          Gustaveson had the birth place of Lars Peter Hollmstrom  as Dalen,    
1 CONC         Ahlstad, Malmohus, Sweden. Our records show the birthplace as Dalen,          Andrarum, Malmohus, Sweden. The Swedish Postal book list over 100             villages named Dalen. There is not one listed in Andrarum, Kristia
1 CONC nstad.
1 CONT There is a village named Dalen in Ahlstad parish in Malmohous.
1 CONT 3-  In my search I found that the compilers of our family records often           inter-changed province and district names for the parish and county. A        Provence is a geographic area established to divide Sweden into  small
1 CONC er      areas, but they have no legal nor clerical capacities, therefoer we will      not able to find records there. How ever many genealogists and family         record keepers have used the Provence as a place of birth. This is
1 CONC             misleading and a stumbling block for searching as the Provence's have no      record to search.
1 CONT
1 CONT An example:  Many of our record compilers have used the place name of  Smaland as the birth of about 20% of our ancestors. After several weeks of frustration I found that Smaland is a Provence in the very  heart of the most popula
1 CONC ted area of Sweden. It covers the lans (counties)  of Kalmar, Jonköping, Kronoberg, and a narrow fringe of most of the  counties surrounding these three counties. Each county has 50 or more  parishes within their boundries. I have
1 CONC  tried to corrected this problem where I found that it was needed, often by comparing the birthplaces of  known relatives.
