0 @N6000000002577169293@ NOTE !SOURCE:
1 CONT 1- 22 Jul 1993: data from the records of Owen B. Anderson
1 CONT 2- 28 Sep 1994: TempleReady file report.
1 CONT
1 CONT !NOTES:
1 CONT 1- 1993: This is a continuing bunch of Family Group Records for the Meurling
1 CONT line that Owen B andeson had in his posession. They all seem to come from     a Swedish Family History collection found in the Family History Library in    Salt Lake City, UT. Some record sheets have a reference to pages in that
1 CONT collection.
1 CONT 2- I have heard that Uncle Arthur- Owen's brother- recieved a batch of           Meurling family records from a researcher in Sweden that she was not able     to fit into owr line, but thought that he would be intrested in them   
1 CONC        anyway. This could be that collection. Maybe when we get them all entered     into our file we will be able to match them up better. Much of the            ordinance work has been done.
1 CONT 3- One thing that makes me feel that these FGR's came from Sweden is that        most of the parishes listed I have been able to find without interpreting     the writing, even though they do not have the Swedish markings.
1 CONT 4- 1994: I am entering a calculated  date of marriage based on the birth date
1 CONT of thier first child. Also, the children were born in Vastervik, where        thier father was born, so am I using that locality for a marriage place.
1 CONT Verificatin will need to come from some parish records.
1 CONT !SOURCE:
1 CONT 1- 22 Jul 1993: data from the records of Owen B. Anderson
1 CONT 2- 28 Sep 1994: TempleReady file report.
1 CONT
1 CONT !NOTES:
1 CONT 1- 1993: This is a continuing bunch of Family Group Records for the Meurling
1 CONT line that Owen B andeson had in his posession. They all seem to come from     a Swedish Family History collection found in the Family History Library in    Salt Lake City, UT. Some record sheets have a reference to pages in that
1 CONT collection.
1 CONT 2- I have heard that Uncle Arthur- Owen's brother- recieved a batch of           Meurling family records from a researcher in Sweden that she was not able     to fit into owr line, but thought that he would be intrested in them   
1 CONC        anyway. This could be that collection. Maybe when we get them all entered     into our file we will be able to match them up better. Much of the            ordinance work has been done.
1 CONT 3- One thing that makes me feel that these FGR's came from Sweden is that        most of the parishes listed I have been able to find without interpreting     the writing, even though they do not have the Swedish markings.
1 CONT 4- 1994: I am entering a calculated  date of marriage based on the birth date
1 CONT of thier first child. Also, the children were born in Vastervik, where        thier father was born, so am I using that locality for a marriage place.
1 CONT Verificatin will need to come from some parish records.
